===Introduction===
'phone rings'
Bruce: Yeah?
Bill: Hey
Bill: How'd it go?
Bruce: Like funerals do
Bill: Anything unexpected?
Bruce: No
Bill: You ok being there alone?
Bruce: I'm just clearing it out; realtor wants it empty for the end of the month
Bill: You don't have to rush it you know
Bruce: I do
Bill: (sighs) Alright, call if it gets heavy
Bruce: It won't
'hangs up'
Bruce: It's just a house
->END
===LivingRoom===
Mother: Turn it sweetheart, the square one
'soft laughter'
Father: There we are, he's got it
->END
===CallOne===
'phone rings'
Bill: You there?
Bruce: Yeah
Bill: How's it feel?
Bruce: Like it never moved on
Bill: And you?
Bruce: I'm fine
'hangs up'
->END
===Kitchen===
Mother: Not too hard, you'll tear it
'gentle laughter'
'front door slams'
Father: Smells good
Mother: We saved you some
->END
===UnderTheStairs===
'muffled arguing'
Father: You think I don't know?
Mother: Lower your voice
Bruce: If i couldn't hear it...
->END
===Window===
Father: What the hell was that?
Bruce: It was an accident
Father: In the hallway? Are you stupid?
Bruce: You've broken worse
Father: Watch your mouth
Bruce: Or what?
Dad: Don't push me boy
Bruce: Some dad you are
Dad: Go to your room, now!
Bruce: I'm not a child
Father: You're acting like one
->END
===DiningRoom===
Father: What do you think you're doing?
Bruce: It's just a bottle
Father: You're just like me
->END
===CallTwo===
Bruce: What?
Bill: You sound wound tight
Bruce: Im handling it
Bill: Handling isn't the same as feeling
Bruce: You don't know what it was like
Bill: No
Bill: But I know what it's like to carry it
->END
===Garage===
Father: Hang up the wrench, would you?
Father: I'm trying, you know
Bruce: Not hard enough!
->END
===Bedroom==
Mother: Bruce, we didn't know how to say this out loud, so we're writing it
Mother: We miss you
Mother: The house feels smaller without you in it
Father: I've stopped drinking son
Father: Should've done it sooner
Mother: You think you disappointed us
Mother: You didn't, you struggled
Father: You saw my worst sides
Father: I'm sorry for that
Father: You don't have to carry them
Mother: If you ever want to come home, the door is never locked
Mother: Even if we aren't here to open it
->END
===CallThree===
Bill: Hey
Bruce: He stopped
Bill: Yeah?
Bruce: I didn't know
Bruce: I thought he never would
Bill: You going to the meeting tomorrow?
Bruce: Yeah
Bill: Good
Bruce: Im still trying
->END

